WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.440
A good README, without starting from a blank file.

00:00:06.523 --> 00:00:07.723
Here's the README builder.

00:00:09.431 --> 00:00:13.391
Open markdrop.in/builder, and give your README a title.

00:00:14.821 --> 00:00:20.881
Pick from forty-nine ready-made sections: installation, usage, contributing, a license, and more.

00:00:21.581 --> 00:00:23.141
Search, or browse by group.

00:00:24.605 --> 00:00:29.725
There are diagrams too, from flowcharts and sequence diagrams to Gantt charts, and math.

00:00:30.345 --> 00:00:32.105
They render in the preview as you go.

00:00:34.299 --> 00:00:38.679
Select a section to edit its Markdown, with the same toolbar as the editor.

00:00:40.879 --> 00:00:45.239
Drag sections into order, and the table of contents rebuilds from the headings.

00:00:47.595 --> 00:00:51.775
When it's ready, copy the Markdown, or download README.md to commit.

00:00:53.626 --> 00:00:57.686
Or publish it as a Markdrop link, with the same settings as any document.

00:01:00.835 --> 00:01:04.695
No account needed, and your work is saved in this browser as you go.

00:01:06.839 --> 00:01:09.859
Build yours at markdrop.in/builder.

00:01:09.879 --> 00:01:10.819
No account needed.
